  "id": "pupillometry",
  "term": "pupillometry",
  "definition": "Pupillometry is a non-invasive, objective method that measures changes in pupil size in real time. In psychology research, it is used as a sensitive way to study cognitive effort and aspects of lexical processing such as word recognition, word retrieval, and semantic activation, although exactly what pupil responses reflect in word processing is not yet fully settled.",
